# Omni Screen Project

## Stack

- **Desktop**: Electron 40
- **Frontend**: React 18, TypeScript 5
- **Build**: Vite 7, vite-plugin-electron
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS 4, DaisyUI 5
- **Other**: D3.js 7, marked, ws

## Structure

- `src/` – React components, utils, assets
- `electron/` – Main process, preload, chat managers, extensions
- `src/assets/media/sound/notification/` – Notification sounds; all .mp3/.wav/.ogg/.m4a/.aac files are auto-detected. Selector shows full filenames (e.g. 534.wav) so same-name different-ext files appear separately.

## Entry Points

- **Renderer**: `src/main.tsx` → `App.tsx` (routes: menu, link-scroller, omni-screen, debug, chat-window)
- **Main**: `electron/main.ts` – IPC, chat WebSockets, platform APIs

## Chat Architecture

- **Primary chat**: `electron/chatWebSocket.ts` – WebSocket to extension's chatWssUrl
- **Platform chats**: `kickChatManager.ts`, `youtubeChatManager.ts`, `twitchChatManager.ts`
- **Live feed**: `electron/liveWebSocket.ts` – embeds, banned list
- **Delivery**: `electron/chatServerWs.ts` – local WebSocket server on `ws://127.0.0.1:5174`. All consumers (main window, chat window, OBS) connect here. Main broadcasts via `broadcastChatMessage`. See `docs/ARCHITECTURE-WEBSOCKETS.md`.
- **Renderer client**: `src/utils/chatWsClient.ts` – `chatWsOn(channel, handler)`, `chatWsSendRegister` / `chatWsSendUnregister`

## Key Components

- `OmniScreen.tsx` – Main screen, embed grid, combined chat pane/overlay
- `CombinedChat.tsx` – Combined feed (primary + Kick + YouTube + Twitch). Primary chat MSG is batched (queue + queueMicrotask flush) to avoid losing messages when many arrive rapidly. Deduplication key: `platform:channel:user:timestamp`. Always ordered by arrival (seq). Primary chat emotes: cache-before-display – preload emote images before appending messages to avoid flash; preload cache cleared on `chat-websocket-reload`. Poll history: button (bar-chart-2) when extension provides `pollsApiUrl` in chatSources; lazy fetch, cached; new POLLSTOP merged; nav arrows + info in header, counter centered below poll; hidden when `hidePinnedAndPollHistory` (OBS embed).
- `LinkScroller.tsx` – Link cards from chat
- `LiteLinkScroller.tsx` – Compact sidebar with LS (links) / RS (RustleSearch) toggle. RustleSearch label links to https://rustlesearch.dev/
- `Menu.tsx` – Settings modal: System, Theme, Notifications, Userscripts (collapsible dropdowns)

## Notifications & Sounds

- **Live checks**: `electron/liveCheckScheduler.ts` – background polls bookmarked streamers with `notifyWhenLive`; triggers sound, OS notification, or in-app toast (when main window focused)
- **Sound playback**: `electron/soundWindow.ts` – hidden BrowserWindow with HTML5 audio; plays from `src/assets/media/sound/notification/` or custom path

## Scripts

- `npm run extract:chat-samples` – Extracts 2–4 samples per type from `logs/chat-history.log` into `logs/chat-samples.json`. Only fills missing data; does not remove existing samples. Used by Debug page "Primary chat message formatting" section.

## Debugging Chat Message Loss

- **chat-history.log**: Enable "Log chat history" in Menu. Primary chat raw messages are written here by `fileLogger.writeChatHistory` in `chatWebSocket.ts` before parsing. If a message is missing from the log, it never reached the main process.
- **Pipeline**: destiny.gg → ChatWebSocket → broadcastChatMessage → chatServerWs (clients) → chatWsClient → CombinedChat handleMessage → appendItems. Drop points: `clients.size === 0` in broadcastChatMessage; handler not registered in chatWsClient; tryAddPrimaryChatMessage dedup; trimToLimit.
- **Debug page "Primary chat message flow"**: Counters at each stage (main received, broadcast sent, wsClient dispatched, CombinedChat received, appended, rejected duplicate). Main process counters in `electron/primaryChatDebugCounters.ts`; renderers push to main for aggregation. Reset and compare during busy chat to find drop point.

## Icon and SVG Usage

- **Icon component** (`src/components/Icon.tsx`): Uses SVGs imported with `?raw` suffix (e.g. `import xSvg from '../assets/icons/feathericons/x.svg?raw'`). SVG content is stored in the `ICONS` map and rendered inline via `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. Icons inherit `text-current` for theme support. Only predefined `IconName` keys are supported.
- **Custom SVG icons** (e.g. LS.svg, RS.svg not in Icon): Use `?url` suffix and `<img>`: `import lsIcon from '../assets/icons/LS.svg?url'` then `<img src={lsIcon} alt="" width={20} height={20} className="..." />`. Vite's `?url` returns the asset URL. Use this when the SVG is not in the Icon component's ICONS map.
- **Adding new Icon names**: Import with `?raw`, add to `ICONS` in Icon.tsx. For SVGs with `fill="#000000"`, add a CSS override (e.g. `[&_*]:fill-current`) so they inherit theme color.

## Conventions

- **No settings migration**: Do not add migration logic for existing user settings. Use new defaults directly; existing users keep their stored values.
- localStorage keys prefixed `omni-screen:`
- IPC channels: `platform-chat-action` (e.g. `kick-chat-set-targets`, `youtube-chat-message`)
- Embed keys: `platform:id` (e.g. `kick:slug`, `youtube:videoId`, `twitch:login`)
- BookmarkedStreamer: `notifyWhenLive` (default false) – per-streamer notification toggle; `openWhenLive` – auto-open embed when live
